{"content_hash": "9291aeb26dba29df", "version_id": 555, "article_id": 56, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize", "title_zh": "加拿大诗人安妮·卡森荣获诺贝尔文学奖", "has_translation": true, "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq4g1j54nepyo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586859411132-573998709aa9?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8Ym9sZCUyMGludmVudGl2ZSUyMGNhbmFkaWFufGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2NzgxOTd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Isabel Piñeiro on Unsplash", "author": "Isabel Piñeiro", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@isabelpinheiro?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/red-and-white-flag-on-rock-formation-near-body-of-water-during-daytime-MJFBzRgEqEc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(250, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(288, 46%, 48%)", "label": "CULTURE", "seed": "45e27dcc686b"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 253, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "The Swedish Academy has awarded the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature to Canadian poet, essayist and translator Anne Carson. The 76-year-old was praised for a body of work that blurs the lines between poetry, fiction and scholarship.", "lead_zh": "瑞典学院将2026年诺贝尔文学奖授予加拿大诗人、散文家兼翻译家安妮·卡森。这位76岁的作家因其模糊诗歌、小说与学术界限的作品而受到表彰。", "preview": "The Swedish Academy on Thursday named Anne Carson, the 76-year-old Canadian poet, essayist and translator, as the winner of the 2026 Nobel P", "preview_zh": "周四，瑞典学院宣布76岁的加拿大诗人、散文家兼翻译家安妮·卡森获得2026年诺贝尔文学奖。委员会在颁奖词中称赞她“大胆而富有创新的作品，在与古典传统的戏谑对话中，为当代文学创造了新的形式”。该奖项表彰终身成就，奖金为1200万瑞典克朗，约合90万英镑。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 543, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/56/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 108.962, "size_bytes": 657504, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 309, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/555.json", "paragraphs": ["The Swedish Academy on Thursday named Anne Carson, the 76-year-old Canadian poet, essayist and translator, as the winner of the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature. In its citation, the committee commended her \"bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\". The prize, awarded for a lifetime's achievement, carries 12 million Swedish kronor, roughly £900,000.", "Reached by public broadcaster RUV in Iceland, where she is currently staying, Carson responded with characteristic wit, joking that the judges were \"crazy\" to honour her. Ingrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said she had broken the news by phone shortly before the announcement. \"She was taken by surprise but very happy,\" Carlberg said. \"I could hear that in her voice.\"", "Born in Toronto in 1950, Carson has lived in Michigan and has held Icelandic citizenship since 2022. Anders Olsson, who chairs the Nobel committee, praised how she has \"broken away from lyrical poetry bound to the narrative self and inspired new forms of contemporary literature\". Her writing, he added, moves playfully between classical and modern poetry as well as across genres and artforms.", "Carson's notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red, Nox, Float and The Beauty of the Husband. Her 2021 graphic retelling of Euripides, The Trojan Women: A Comic, and a London staging of her Sophocles translation Elektra, starring Brie Larson, illustrate her genre-crossing range. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called the win \"an extraordinary achievement and a proud moment for Canada\"."], "paragraphs_zh": ["周四，瑞典学院宣布76岁的加拿大诗人、散文家兼翻译家安妮·卡森获得2026年诺贝尔文学奖。委员会在颁奖词中称赞她“大胆而富有创新的作品，在与古典传统的戏谑对话中，为当代文学创造了新的形式”。该奖项表彰终身成就，奖金为1200万瑞典克朗，约合90万英镑。", "卡森目前身在冰岛，她在接受公共广播公司RUV采访时以一贯的机智回应，开玩笑说评委们授予她这一荣誉简直是“疯了”。瑞典学院常任秘书英格丽德·卡尔伯格表示，她在公开宣布前不久通过电话将消息告诉了卡森。卡尔伯格说：“她感到很意外，但非常高兴。我从她的声音里能听出来。”", "卡森1950年出生于多伦多，现居密歇根州，自2022年起还拥有冰岛国籍。诺贝尔委员会主席安德斯·奥尔松称赞她“摆脱了受叙事自我束缚的抒情诗，激发了当代文学的新形式”。他补充说，她的写作在古典与现代诗歌之间、在不同体裁和艺术形式之间嬉戏游走。", "卡森的代表作包括《玻璃随笔》《红色自传》《夜》《漂浮》和《丈夫的美：29首探戈中的虚构散文》。她2021年对欧里庇得斯的图像小说式重述《特洛伊妇女：漫画》，以及去年在伦敦上演、由布丽·拉尔森主演的索福克勒斯《厄勒克特拉》译本，都展现了她跨越体裁的广度。加拿大总理马克·卡尼称这一获奖是“非凡的成就，是加拿大的骄傲时刻”。"], "body": "The Swedish Academy on Thursday named Anne Carson, the 76-year-old Canadian poet, essayist and translator, as the winner of the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature. In its citation, the committee commended her \"bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\". The prize, awarded for a lifetime's achievement, carries 12 million Swedish kronor, roughly £900,000.\n\nReached by public broadcaster RUV in Iceland, where she is currently staying, Carson responded with characteristic wit, joking that the judges were \"crazy\" to honour her. Ingrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said she had broken the news by phone shortly before the announcement. \"She was taken by surprise but very happy,\" Carlberg said. \"I could hear that in her voice.\"\n\nBorn in Toronto in 1950, Carson has lived in Michigan and has held Icelandic citizenship since 2022. Anders Olsson, who chairs the Nobel committee, praised how she has \"broken away from lyrical poetry bound to the narrative self and inspired new forms of contemporary literature\". Her writing, he added, moves playfully between classical and modern poetry as well as across genres and artforms.\n\nCarson's notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red, Nox, Float and The Beauty of the Husband. Her 2021 graphic retelling of Euripides, The Trojan Women: A Comic, and a London staging of her Sophocles translation Elektra, starring Brie Larson, illustrate her genre-crossing range. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called the win \"an extraordinary achievement and a proud moment for Canada\".", "body_zh": "周四，瑞典学院宣布76岁的加拿大诗人、散文家兼翻译家安妮·卡森获得2026年诺贝尔文学奖。委员会在颁奖词中称赞她“大胆而富有创新的作品，在与古典传统的戏谑对话中，为当代文学创造了新的形式”。该奖项表彰终身成就，奖金为1200万瑞典克朗，约合90万英镑。\n\n卡森目前身在冰岛，她在接受公共广播公司RUV采访时以一贯的机智回应，开玩笑说评委们授予她这一荣誉简直是“疯了”。瑞典学院常任秘书英格丽德·卡尔伯格表示，她在公开宣布前不久通过电话将消息告诉了卡森。卡尔伯格说：“她感到很意外，但非常高兴。我从她的声音里能听出来。”\n\n卡森1950年出生于多伦多，现居密歇根州，自2022年起还拥有冰岛国籍。诺贝尔委员会主席安德斯·奥尔松称赞她“摆脱了受叙事自我束缚的抒情诗，激发了当代文学的新形式”。他补充说，她的写作在古典与现代诗歌之间、在不同体裁和艺术形式之间嬉戏游走。\n\n卡森的代表作包括《玻璃随笔》《红色自传》《夜》《漂浮》和《丈夫的美：29首探戈中的虚构散文》。她2021年对欧里庇得斯的图像小说式重述《特洛伊妇女：漫画》，以及去年在伦敦上演、由布丽·拉尔森主演的索福克勒斯《厄勒克特拉》译本，都展现了她跨越体裁的广度。加拿大总理马克·卡尼称这一获奖是“非凡的成就，是加拿大的骄傲时刻”。", "text": "The Swedish Academy on Thursday named Anne Carson, the 76-year-old Canadian poet, essayist and translator, as the winner of the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature. In its citation, the committee commended her \"bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\". The prize, awarded for a lifetime's achievement, carries 12 million Swedish kronor, roughly £900,000. Reached by public broadcaster RUV in Iceland, where she is currently staying, Carson responded with characteristic wit, joking that the judges were \"crazy\" to honour her. Ingrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said she had broken the news by phone shortly before the announcement. \"She was taken by surprise but very happy,\" Carlberg said. \"I could hear that in her voice.\" Born in Toronto in 1950, Carson has lived in Michigan and has held Icelandic citizenship since 2022. Anders Olsson, who chairs the Nobel committee, praised how she has \"broken away from lyrical poetry bound to the narrative self and inspired new forms of contemporary literature\". Her writing, he added, moves playfully between classical and modern poetry as well as across genres and artforms. Carson's notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red, Nox, Float and The Beauty of the Husband. Her 2021 graphic retelling of Euripides, The Trojan Women: A Comic, and a London staging of her Sophocles translation Elektra, starring Brie Larson, illustrate her genre-crossing range. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney called the win \"an extraordinary achievement and a proud moment for Canada\".", "vocab": [{"word": "oeuvre", "pos": "noun", "zh": "全部作品；作品集", "note": "正式用语，指某位作家或艺术家的整体创作。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "commend", "pos": "verb", "zh": "称赞；表扬", "note": "比 praise 更正式，常用于官方或书面语境。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "citation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "颁奖词；引文", "note": "此处指颁奖机构对获奖者的评价文字。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "playful", "pos": "adj", "zh": "戏谑的；顽皮的", "note": "形容风格轻松、不严肃。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "break the news", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "告知消息（尤指坏消息或重大消息）", "note": "固定搭配，常与 to 连用。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "permanent secretary", "pos": "noun", "zh": "常任秘书", "note": "瑞典学院等机构的最高行政职位。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "wit", "pos": "noun", "zh": "机智；风趣", "note": "常指说话或写作中的幽默才智。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "genre", "pos": "noun", "zh": "体裁；类型", "note": "文学、艺术等的分类。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "graphic retelling", "pos": "noun", "zh": "图像小说式重述", "note": "用漫画或图像形式重新讲述故事。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "staging", "pos": "noun", "zh": "上演；舞台呈现", "note": "指戏剧的演出制作。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "genre-crossing", "pos": "adj", "zh": "跨体裁的", "note": "形容跨越不同艺术或文学类型。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "lyrical", "pos": "adj", "zh": "抒情的", "note": "常形容诗歌或文字富有情感和音乐性。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "contemporary", "pos": "adj", "zh": "当代的", "note": "指当今或近期的。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "outstanding", "pos": "adj", "zh": "杰出的；突出的", "note": "常用于正式评价，表示卓越。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "'Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize", "summary_original": "Carson, 76, is celebrated for works that often cross boundaries between poetry, fiction and scholarship.", "body_original": "'Bold and inventive' Canadian poet Anne Carson wins Nobel Literature Prize\nBy\nIan Youngs\nCulture reporter\nPublished\n8 October 2026\nCanadian poet, essayist and translator Anne Carson has been awarded this year's Nobel Prize in Literature.\nCarson, 76, is celebrated for works that often cross the boundaries between poetry, fiction and scholarship.\nThe Nobel Prize committee said they had selected her \"for her bold and inventive oeuvre that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for contemporary literature\".\nCarson responded by joking that the judges were \"crazy\" for honouring her. \"I think they're all crazy... Well, you know, it's crazy,\" she told public broadcaster RUV in Iceland, where she is currently staying.\nThe Nobel Prize is awarded for a lifetime's body of work and is regarded as the most prestigious award in global literature, with the winner receiving 12 million Swedish kronor (£900,000, $1.2m).\nIngrid Carlberg, permanent secretary of the Swedish Academy, said she had broken the news to Carson on the phone shortly before the public announcement.\n\"She had time to tell me was that she is, for the moment, in Iceland, where she is listening to the wind,\" Carlberg, said.\n\"She was taken by surprise but very happy. I could hear that in her voice.\"\nBorn in Toronto in 1950, Carson lives in Michigan and has also held Icelandic citizenship since 2022.\nAnders Olsson, chairman of the Swedish Academy's Nobel committee for Literature, praised the way Carson has \"broken away from lyrical poetry bound to the narrative self and inspired new forms of contemporary literature\".\n\"This method of writing leads to playful and ironic works that move not only between classical and modern poetry but also between different genres and artforms,\" he said.\nCanadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said Carson's win was \"an extraordinary achievement and a proud moment for Canada\".\nThe writer's works feature \"wit, imagination, and a style entirely her own,\" Carney wrote on social media.\n\"She has brought ancient stories to new audiences and transformed the way we think about literature.\"\n'Outstanding importance'\nCarson's notable works include The Glass Essay, Autobiography of Red: A Novel in Verse, Nox, Float and The Beauty of the Husband: A Fictional Essay in 29 Tangos.\nIn 2019, her performance piece Norma Jeane Baker of Troy drew a line between famous beauties from different historical periouds - Helen of Troy and Marilyn Monroe.\nIn 2021, she released The Trojan Women: A Comic, a graphic retelling of Euripides' ancient story; and her translation of Elektra by Sophocles was staged starring Brie Larson in London last year.\nShe has been a professor of classics for more than 30 years and her writing is often inspired by Greek literature.\nHer translations have often given a contemporary twist to ancient works.\n\"Her collaborations with visual artists and choreographers and with opera and theatre directors demonstrate the freedom with which she relates to literary expectations and rule systems,\" Olsson said.\n\"It is this that lies behind the outstanding importance her work since the 1990s has had for the international art and literature scene.\"\nRelated topics\nBooks\nLiterature\nNobel Prize\nMore on this story\nHungarian author László Krasznahorkai wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n9 October 2025\nSouth Korea's Han Kang wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n10 October 2024\nNorway's Jon Fosse wins Nobel Literature Prize\nPublished\n5 October 2023", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:23:16.183990", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.275, "sm": 100, "em": 275, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Swedish", "s": 0.287, "e": 0.7, "sm": 287, "em": 700, "cs": 4, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 